        <updated>2026-10-26T21:11:22.344Z</updated>
        <content type="html"><![CDATA[<div class="Story_container"><div class="Story_data"><div class="Story_title"><a href="https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50234474"><span>Dolly Parton's Imagination Library</span></a><a href="https://imaginationlibrary.com/" target="_blank" class="Story_link">(https://imaginationlibrary.com/)</a></div><div class="Story_meta"><span><a href="https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50234474">682 points</a></span><span class="Story_separator">|</span><span><a href="https://news.ycombinator.com/user?id=jumploops"><span>jumploops</span></a></span><span class="Story_separator">|</span><span><a href="https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50234474">4 days ago</a></span><span class="Story_separator">|</span><span><a href="https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50234474">111 comments</a></span><div class="Story_comment"><span>With today's news, I thought I'd share this great program:<p>“When I was growing up in the hills of East Tennessee, I knew my dreams would come true. I know there are children in your community with their own dreams. They dream of becoming a doctor or an inventor or a minister. Who knows, maybe there is a little girl whose dream is to be a writer and singer.</p><p>The seeds of these dreams are often found in books and the seeds you help plant in your community can grow across the world.”</p></span></div></div></div></div>]]></content>
